1
00:00:02,737 --> 00:00:08,440
This is Tech and Sci-Fi Books, a personal book manager built from small Bash programs.

2
00:00:08,440 --> 00:00:12,242
The Gum interface makes it easy to organize a reading

3
00:00:12,242 --> 00:00:16,424
list and explore recommendations for programming, artificial intelligence, and science fiction.

4
00:00:17,127 --> 00:00:19,893
First, I will add Dune by Frank Herbert.

5
00:00:19,893 --> 00:00:23,005
The app searches Open Library and returns matching books.

6
00:00:23,005 --> 00:00:28,193
Instead of typing every detail, I can choose the correct result and review its metadata.

7
00:00:28,898 --> 00:00:34,567
I confirm the title, author, genre, and link, then keep the status as want to read.

8
00:00:34,567 --> 00:00:39,527
After I approve the entry, the database component saves it to a CSV file.

9
00:00:39,527 --> 00:00:41,653
Each layer has a separate responsibility.

10
00:00:42,356 --> 00:00:44,772
Next, I search for Frank Herbert.

11
00:00:44,772 --> 00:00:48,798
The saved book appears immediately, along with its reading status.

12
00:00:48,798 --> 00:00:55,239
Search works across titles, authors, and genres, and the library stays available after the app closes.

13
00:00:55,943 --> 00:00:57,577
Finally, I request recommendations.

14
00:00:57,577 --> 00:01:04,520
The starting interests are programming, AI, and science fiction, and I can change them for this run.

15
00:01:04,520 --> 00:01:09,830
The app will send the same library snapshot to three independent recommendation strategies.

16
00:01:10,534 --> 00:01:14,174
All three strategies are now running at the same time.

17
00:01:14,174 --> 00:01:16,358
History uses saved books and ratings.

18
00:01:16,358 --> 00:01:18,543
Interests follows the topics I entered.

19
00:01:18,543 --> 00:01:20,727
Discovery explores outside the usual pattern.

20
00:01:20,727 --> 00:01:26,187
The status messages show each task finishing, while the Bash workflow waits for every process.

21
00:01:26,888 --> 00:01:30,127
The workflow combines the results and pipes them into refinement.

22
00:01:30,127 --> 00:01:36,607
That step removes duplicates and books already in the library, then rotates among the strategies to produce a short list.

23
00:01:36,607 --> 00:01:40,170
Each suggestion shows its source and a reason for reading it.

24
00:01:40,873 --> 00:01:46,655
That is the complete demo: adding a book, searching the library, and generating recommendations.

25
00:01:46,655 --> 00:01:50,784
Small Bash files handle the layers, Gum handles interaction, and

26
00:01:50,784 --> 00:01:54,501
parallel processes and a pipe connect the recommendation workflow.
